WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.470
-After four years of spewing
racist, anti-immigrant vitriol,

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.239
President Trump read a scripted
denunciation of racism

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:09.042
off the teleprompter yesterday,

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.677
so the New York Times decided
to go with this banner headline,

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:14.213
"Trump Urges Unity Vs. Racism."

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:16.649
The<i> Times</i> later admitted the
headline was flawed

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.651
and changed it
for subsequent editions,

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.054
which brings us to a segment
called "Hey!"

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:24.224
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:27.093
All right, let's take a look

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.895
at a few seconds
of Trump urging unity.

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:33.833
-In one voice,
our nation must condemn racism,

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.404
bigotry, and white supremacy.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:41.541
These sinister ideologies
must be defeated.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.709
Hate has no place in America.

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.545
-Hey, it doesn't really sound

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.313
like he was speaking
from his heart.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.815
I mean, even the painting of
George Washington behind him

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:51.317
wasn't buying it.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.786
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.755
You can't say
someone urged something

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:58.357
when they do it completely
without urgency.

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:00.560
He's already back
to quoting Fox News

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.561
and attacking people
on Twitter again today.

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:03.796
A better headline would've been

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:07.466
"Teleprompter Urges Unity
While Old Man Watches."

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:09.002
I mean, hey,<i> New York Times,</i>

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.571
is Trump writing
your headlines now?

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.973
The only thing missing
from that were the typos.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.875
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.777
You're supposed to be
the paper of record,

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.012
not the paper
of record scratches.

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:21.547
"Trump urges unity?!"

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:23.216
[ Record scratches ]

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:27.186
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.455
Hey,<i> New York Times,</i>
we depend on you.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:31.957
We need you
to learn the lessons of 2016,

00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:34.293
and one of them is
"Don't just uncritically repeat

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:36.862
whatever this president
reads off a teleprompter,"

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:38.331
because he never means it.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.400
I mean, the real Trump always
comes out later in his tweets

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.702
or his rallies
or during full moons.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.270
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.504
This headline was so weird,

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:47.840
it was like when you read
a newspaper left behind

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.875
by a time traveller
in a sci-fi movie

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:52.277
and realize you're
in an alternate timeline.

00:01:52.277 --> 00:01:53.946
"Trump Urges Unity"?!

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:56.482
"Cleveland Browns
Win Super Bowl"?!

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:57.884
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.452
Look,<i> New York Times,</i>
we love you.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:02.088
We depend on you, and that's why
we need you to do better.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.023
I'm not saying
you'll never make mistakes,

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:06.125
I'm just hoping you'll get wise
to Trump's act,

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:09.195
and when you do, I look forward
to reading the headline,

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.363
"New York Times
Wakes the [Bleep] Up."

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:14.067
This has been "Hey!"

